  "body": "PR2825's numerical envelope assumed successful `Consumer.apply` execution; PR2835 removed that premise only for closed coefficient calls. This package proves the remaining non-coefficient allocation-prefix effects for unchanged PR2697 and composes them with PR2835. With all entry live residents L and allocated backing K counted, capacities `C_R >= max(K_R,L_R+37672)` and `C_I >= max(K_I,L_I+41)` exclude a first numerical inventory failure. Setup's transient nine indices and the fallback child's retained zero half-width Word remain explicitly charged.\n\nThe result is a **conditional all-parameter written source proof** for dimension 64, widths 64\u2013127, ranks 1\u201342 and admitted finite programs/fields. Semantic validity/termination, PR2835's closed-coefficient prefix/restoration contracts, distinct canonical arenas and numerical-neutral external providers remain premises. This is not selected catalogue admission, a physical/recursive/outer reserve, a formal-kernel proof or a new kappa.\n\nOnly `research/selected-caller-capacity-prefix/` is added at `e053f223c5e225554130572b1af4f329068ec7aa`. Frozen PR2825 source/harness and PR2831/2835 proof exports retain exact pins and notices. Credit Jose Manuel/jmbarrancoml, Nick Petalas, Arham Tahir, Ross Richardson, David Arias, ywz65, starship-s and retained source lineage. Substantial OpenAI Codex assistance includes a separate mathematical AI audit; no independent human review is claimed.\n\nValidation:\n- Registered CPython 3.12 and read-only Git-free optimized CPython 3.14: all three commands pass; final computational bytes match the portable export.\n- Primary: 2,720,449 pending requests, three caller probes, ten complete small Boolean ADD/swap/sign fixtures, five actual quota failures and eight defect-control groups. Caller probes reuse the credited harness and abstract coefficient bodies/full GL64 payload; synthetic 22-index child scratch tests composition only.\n- Separate implementation: fifteen positive fixtures, thirteen actual one-slot-short failures and 37,040 trace events; no verifier imports. Full scope and commands are in VALIDATION.md and INDEPENDENT.md.\n\n**Upstream check history, now resolved:** clean entry/submission main failed `research_baseline.py` after `2dfb25cd` changed `verify_hpe_lean_binding.py` to explicit UTF-8 loading without its selected-record digest. Final canonical refresh at 01:58:46 UTC picked up maintainer commit `d359705715f45a25d46c593a542e8d071c47160a`, which updates that digest; `PASS_RESEARCH_BASELINE_BINDINGS_ONLY` now passes. The frozen package records the earlier failure truthfully, uses neither that supplement nor the selected finite certificate as a caller-proof premise, and changes no selected record. No full selected replay or hosted CI pass is claimed.\n\nSubmission main `8dc7cef9` refreshed at 01:38 UTC, priority 5/guidance/selected/runner unchanged. Complete metadata overlap through 01:42 UTC covers 620 open PRs, 1484 Discussion records and 2266 local records; arbitrary diffs/unpublished work remain outside coverage. [Canonical claim](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2319#discussioncomment-18962353). Next: join numerical backing with the other storage categories at common chronological cuts and bind physical grants.\n\nFinal housekeeping: all 63 public files match the exact tested head, the claim is released, the retained branch/bundle/patch/ZIP are verified, and the completed owned worktree/scratch were removed. Scientific pins remain unchanged; final selected-record hash is `bb2eaa58647b353f88d0aec2eafb9d30df1be53589231b23e12ceef3e4bad129`.\n",
